.TH SSHM 1 "2026-06-09" "SSH Manager v0.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sshm \- SSH connection manager with interactive TUI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sshm
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIkeyword\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
SSH Manager is a terminal-based SSH connection management tool.
It wraps \fBexpect\fR(1) to automate password and key-based authentication.
.SH USAGE
.SS Interactive mode
.PP
Run \fBsshm\fR without arguments to enter the interactive list view.
.TP
.B \(ua \(da
Navigate between nodes (selected row is highlighted)
.TP
.B Enter
Connect to the selected node
.TP
.B Type
Filter nodes in real-time by name or host
.TP
.B ESC
Clear current filter
.TP
.B s
Cycle sort mode: by group, by name, by status
.TP
.B a
Add a new node
.TP
.B d
Toggle delete mode (select node with Enter to delete)
.TP
.B e / i
Export/import configuration (base64 or file)
.TP
.B r
Show recent connections history
.TP
.B h
Show help
.TP
.B q
Quit
.TP
.B Ctrl+C
Clear filter and return to top of list
.SS Command-line direct connect
.PP
\fBsshm \fIkeyword\fR
Search nodes by keyword. If exactly one match, connect directly.
If multiple matches, list them with details.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h , " --help"
Show help message and exit
.TP
.BR \-v , " --version"
Show version and exit
.TP
.BI \-\-config " file"
Use specified YAML config file
.TP
.B \-\-validate
Validate config file syntax and report node count
.TP
.BI \-\-import-ssh-config " file"
Import Host entries from \fB~/.ssh/config\fP format
.SH CONFIGURATION
.SS File format
YAML file with a top-level \fBnodes:\fP list:
.PP
.nf
nodes:
  \- name: myserver
    group: Production
    host: 192.168.1.100
    port: 22
    user: admin
    type: pass
    pass: "password"
.fi
.PP
For key-based auth, use \fBtype: key\fP and specify \fBkeypath\fP.
.SS Config file priority
.TP
1.
\fB\-\-config\fP command-line argument
.TP
2.
\fBSSH_MANAGER_CONFIG\fP environment variable
.TP
3.
\fB~/.config/ssh-manager/config.yaml\fP (recommended)
.TP
4.
\fB/etc/ssh-manager/config.yaml\fP
.TP
5.
\fB./config.yaml\fP (current directory)
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/ssh-manager/config.yaml
Default user configuration file
.TP
.I ~/.cache/ssh-manager-history
Recent connection history (last 10)
.TP
.I /etc/ssh-manager/config.yaml
System-wide default configuration
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SSH_MANAGER_CONFIG
Override default config file path
.SH SHELL COMPLETION
.PP
Bash: \fBsource /usr/share/bash-completion/completions/sshm\fP
.br
Zsh:  automatically loaded from \fB/usr/share/zsh/site-functions/_sshm\fP
.br
Fish: \fBsource /usr/share/fish/vendor_completions.d/sshm.fish\fP
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ssh (1),
.BR expect (1),
.BR ssh-keygen (1)
